{% comment %}
Stage 1 — one yes/no per (step, module): "does this step use this module?"

Every step is asked about every module, in ONE exchange. That is the point of the decider: each
answer is independent, so a step using three modules simply gets three yeses rather than the model
having to rank them against each other.

The question points at the state by PATH and never restates the step text — the state was already
handed over, and repeating it would let the wording of one question colour another.

The id is `s<step>_<module>` so the answers can be matched back.
{% endcomment %}
{
  {%- assign sep = "" -%}
  {%- for s in goal.Step -%}
  {%- for m in modules -%}
  {{ sep }}"s{{ s.Index }}_{{ m.Name }}": {
    "type": "noul",
    "instructions": "Does `steps[{{ s.Index }}].text` use the plang module `{{ m.Name }}` (described at `modules.{{ m.Name }}`) to do what it says?"
  }
  {%- assign sep = "," -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
}
